      <p><strong>Terrain relief:</strong> hillshade makes ridges, hollows and cliffs easier to recognize.</p>
      <p><strong>Sunrise / Sunset Potential:</strong> terrain-only estimate above 1,100 ft. Solid coral/indigo starts at directional exposed rims and fades toward the local ridge crest. “Potential” means likely exposure, not guaranteed access, safety, standing room, vegetation clearance, or a usable viewpoint.</p>
      <p><strong>Aerial:</strong> shows visible ground features when photographed; it does not establish public access.</p>
      <p><strong>Official trails:</strong> magenta pill-dashed lines show Kentucky State Park trails; bright cyan pill-dashed lines show USDA Forest Service trails. Where the two overlap, the State Park trail is drawn on top.</p>
      <p><strong>RRGH routes:</strong> thick, individually colored highlighted lines for hikes documented by Red River Gorge Hiker.</p>
      <p><strong>Community / informal trails:</strong> light dashed lines with a dark casing, kept visually separate from official trails, roads, land-management boundaries, and the solid RRGH route palette.</p>
      <p><strong>Roads:</strong> bright yellow pill-dashed lines show Forest Service roads. In Terrain or Aerial view, optional thin muted lines show Local / old roads from Census TIGERweb plus cached OpenStreetMap road context at close zoom. Their status is uncertain; they are roads, not trails, and may be abandoned, gated, closed, or no longer passable.</p>
    </div>
